{
  "reviews": [
    {
      "actor": "ash-1",
      "decision": "develop",
      "ability": null,
      "reason": "The requested effect is a read-only, site-specific explanation of the actual tray placement rules and observed interference. Generic probing does not provide that complete construction assessment. Existing root-surface diagnostics concern a different preparation surface, while root-small-drying assesses a different structure with different material and geometry requirements. Develop the smallest diagnostic extension to root-air-drying, reusing its actual placement validator rather than inventing a second clearance model. The supplied evidence does not establish which objects caused the previous failures.",
      "specification": "Implement root-tray-clearance@1, interface root-tray-clearance, prerequisite root-air-drying; individual learning 1 round. Public input: {mode:'assess'|'read', site?:{x:number,y:number}, angle?:number, assessmentId?:string}; assess requires finite in-bounds coordinates, angle defaults to the construction interface's actual default, and read requires an owned retained assessment ID. Shared references: current actor identity/body geometry, world coordinates and units, root-air-drying construction geometry and placement predicates, interaction=0.65, vision=5, current visibility/occlusion, world bounds, collision layers and surface reservations. Extract the existing tray placement checks into a shared pure evaluator used by both construction and assessment; record this code reuse separately from the new diagnostic function. Preserve existing placement semantics, material requirements and construction costs. Assessment costs one active round and 0.2 energy, with no materials, escrow, reservations, movement or construction. Require the candidate footprint to be locally observable; return unknown for unobservable portions rather than revealing concealed entities or certifying clearance. Return a dated assessment with contract revision, site/orientation, actual transformed footprint and work/contact areas, required actor reach/position constraints, and independent pass/fail/unknown results for every applicable placement predicate. For each observed interfering entity report exact public identity, observed geometry, intersection/contact evidence and the predicate it violates; explicitly distinguish the requester, other actors, plants, obstacles, existing facilities and observable reservations. A nonsolid plant is not a blocker unless the actual construction rule treats it as one. Include tested-versus-required distances and clearance values where applicable. Failed assessment reports all observable checks, not merely the first failure; material availability is not a prerequisite for geometry inspection. Never infer unseen blockers from a generic prior failure. Store bounded immutable personal assessment records with normal retention limits; reads cost one round and 0.2 energy and clearly show that results are historical. Construction always revalidates live state and does not accept an assessment as a reservation or guarantee. Declare events tray-clearance-assessed and tray-clearance-read, binding payloads to the public report; optionally emit existing information-confirmed only under its established qualification rules. Execution contract: validate input and affordability before payment; complete an assessment atomically against the execution-round snapshot, exposing completed status and remainingWork=0; pending actions expose remainingWork=1. Cancellation or death before execution cancels without payment or result; after completion no rollback occurs. No escrow exists and nothing is cloned, deleted or transferred. Dependencies are the existing tray validator, shared geometry/visibility, event validation and personal records. Migration is additive: retain all existing objects, rules and mastery, register the new interface/events and assessment schema, and create no tray, stock or personal mastery. Review and development advance no simulation time.",
      "experienceReview": "A successful inspection can provide the applicant with grounded understanding of an encountered obstruction, but requesting the interface, learning it, reading an old result or repeatedly checking an unchanged site earns nothing. Subscribe information-confirmed from root-tray-clearance to the existing grounded-understanding source, not a new alias: participant is the inspecting actor; qualified=true requires a completed paid observation establishing personally new, directly observed placement information with retained evidence. Use the existing transient amount 0.8, cap 1, duration 8 rounds, refresh repetition and 12-round cooldown. Use the same source's maintained gain 0.035 per qualifying event and decay 0.0015 per round, bounded by its existing saturation and global mental limits. Unchanged facts do not qualify again; genuine newly observed changes can. Diagnostic success alone grants no separate practice or mastery reward. There is no direct health, hunger, temperature or physical-comfort effect, and protected mental accounts remain unchanged.",
      "visualReview": "On tray-clearance-assessed, display a temporary nonphysical outline of the actual proposed tray footprint and work/contact regions, with distinct pass/fail/unknown markings. Highlight only observed intersecting geometry and label the relevant requirement, evidence time and measured clearance. Bind the overlay to the dated assessment, never to a fabricated tray entity; it has no collision or reservation effect. Historical reads visibly retain their original timestamp. Replay reconstructs the paid observation and its overlay from the recorded public geometry and checks, without exposing later state or hidden objects."
    ,
      "learning": 1
    }
  ]
}

